82 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393324 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9ee90a69-8fe7-5272-8b17-1772dc5a0e90" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393325 #edb/ref 1080 "images/89/89b88f56878aeb33afe775e083c3775aaa701b6d293ca62e0bd3f2a78923159a.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393325 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393325 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e95ca3e9-ccf0-585e-a54f-3195d2e34519" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393326 #edb/ref 1080 "images/1a/1a7c98897aa0c13daff168b3804ac292c7662ee21f313ddd9e631019bcfbb814.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393326 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393326 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1d979614-76c4-5da3-9edd-dc0cf04890c3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396318 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186396319 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396318 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186396324 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396318 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186396328 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396318 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186396332 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396318 #edb/ref 1069 "q-331821" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396318 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396318 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider a function $b(t)$ such that its Laplace transform is $L{b(t)}=B(s)$ for $s>{s}_{0}.$ Suppose we wish to find $L{{e}^{t}b(t)}.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.By definition of the Laplace transform, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{t}b(t)}&={\\int}_{0}^{\\infty}{{field-1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\&={\\int}_{0}^{\\infty}{{field-2}}b(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\&={{field-3}}\\quad\\text{for }{{field-4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396318 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "276a712f-2260-5901-9134-cf67e08a10a4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396318 #edb/ref 1074 "Starting from the definition of the Laplace transform, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{t}b(t)} & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\cdot {e}^{t}\\,b(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-(s-1)t}\\,b(t)\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $B(s)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\,b(t)\\,\\text{d}t,$ where $s>{s}_{0}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-(s-1)t}\\,b(t)\\,\\text{d}t=B(s-1),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\ns-1>{s}_{0}\\,⇒\\,s>{s}_{0}+1.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396319 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396320 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396319 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396321 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396319 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396322 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396319 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396323 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396319 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396319 #edb/ref 1077 "field-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396319 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186396320 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396319 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d858d9ef-a7c9-5447-928a-43ac88428e2c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396320 #edb/ref 1080 "{e}^{-(s-1)t}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396320 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396320 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "565d4699-585c-59ff-8946-cbdc268b0c14" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396321 #edb/ref 1080 "{e}^{(s-1)t}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396321 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396321 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2f34b198-133c-5315-a86b-d31d8a6f1738" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396322 #edb/ref 1080 "{e}^{(s+1)t}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396322 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396322 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "dfc0db2c-91be-581b-800f-9ebf7f1c9be0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396323 #edb/ref 1080 "{e}^{-(s+1)t}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396323 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396323 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "cc5232e1-5fa0-5561-93b3-19